                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d047c2b5-f704-3766-966e-a211247bcbc5",
                        "entry_id": "d1a922a4-1617-33d1-b66f-b3082fa66689",
                        "glosses": [
                            "лингв. относящийся к несовершенному виду глагола, также к глаголу (глаголам) несовершенного вида"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e37b58c2-3d05-4f54-9a42-ed494e3a2af2",
                        "source_entry_id": "d1a922a4-1617-33d1-b66f-b3082fa66689",
                        "source_sense_id": "d047c2b5-f704-3766-966e-a211247bcbc5",
                        "target_lang_word": "imperfective",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "imperfective",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "01dee220-5535-31aa-a1b9-27d9e3a8f3fd",
                                        "entry_id": "cc0311d0-91c0-3e2e-90f8-6c0aa7d7a822",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, relating to or having the properties of the imperfective aspect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f7c121e-cc53-45b5-a2c5-76647ba54c0b",
                                                "sense_id": "01dee220-5535-31aa-a1b9-27d9e3a8f3fd",
                                                "text": "In the last chapter, we observed the rise of an imperfective marker in English, the Progressive, as the dominant and surviving member of a wider paradigm of imperfective aspectual functions in Old English, but which were no longer marked in the same way in later stages of the history of English."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0784bdac-b5ad-43af-aeda-4e21ad5bb6f0",
                                                "sense_id": "01dee220-5535-31aa-a1b9-27d9e3a8f3fd",
                                                "text": "The former is the basic imperfective subjunctive, while the latter is prominent or intensified.[…]While the present subjunctive is imperfective in aspect, the perfect subjunctive is imperfective in aspect and spatially proximate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcd7fe67-9505-4d4e-8529-8c778a2329f6",
                                                "sense_id": "01dee220-5535-31aa-a1b9-27d9e3a8f3fd",
                                                "text": "Consider, then, the result of applying these tense morphemes to a perfective or an imperfective verb."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "imperfective",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f51b7040-5370-3a64-83ad-2845298117a9",
                                        "entry_id": "e55014c0-fb24-383d-972b-13f3da0bccda",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The imperfective aspect; a verb having this aspect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ece5231-d492-4506-922d-24749f2ad55e",
                                                "sense_id": "f51b7040-5370-3a64-83ad-2845298117a9",
                                                "text": "Examples of past imperfectives are shown in (42)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d18e5931-4a59-434a-bebd-85c690241197",
                                                "sense_id": "f51b7040-5370-3a64-83ad-2845298117a9",
                                                "text": "These putative indeterminate imperfectives are innovative in form precisely because they add a manner meaning to the range of lexical meanings available to Proto-Slavic motion verbs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f15bcc9-408e-4b26-b660-d68cb0772c14",
                                                "sense_id": "f51b7040-5370-3a64-83ad-2845298117a9",
                                                "text": "Past imperfectives are also unproblematic because imperfectives are mass-like in nature, hence contractible."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bb1b6c68-a9d4-4f3b-9424-49c42047ea06",
                        "source_entry_id": "d1a922a4-1617-33d1-b66f-b3082fa66689",
                        "source_sense_id": "d047c2b5-f704-3766-966e-a211247bcbc5",
